. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * Please add a verbal description of your model here
. 
.         * I refrain from using the alternative specification using a 2SLS IV-
> regression, as I have serious concerns about the exclusion restriction being 
> violated. Thus, I stick with the main specification: linear OLS regression
. 
.         * Having Daughters (Daughters) leads to stronger more Left-Leaning po
> litical preferences (LeftLeaning).
.         * Accordingly, we run a linear OLS regression analysis with LeftLeani
> ng as dependent variable and the dummy variable Daughters as independent vari
> able, additionally controlling for total number of children (sumkids), income
>  (hghinc), education (pgbilzeit), marital status (partner), migration backgro
> und (migback), male (male) using heteroskedasticity robus standard errors
. 
.         regress LeftLeaning Daughters sumkids hghinc pgbilzeit ib1.partner ib
> 1.migback i.male, robust

